## Goal
Fix DEV-25: `portero default set` failed after the macOS dialog had already set both schemes. The commit also makes `make install` ship the current build and gives a clearer error when a scheme has no handler.

## Problems
- QA failed the first pass. The installed app was an old bundle (revision 08e28ca) without the fix.
- Cause: `scripts/install.sh` rebuilt only when `build/Portero.app` was missing, so it copied a stale bundle.
- The stale bundle would have made the user's live `default set` run the old code.
- Minor finding: an empty handler from `current()` produced `still handled by ""`, which reads badly.
- The code change itself passed vet, tests, the Linux build and the status output check.

## Decision
- `install.sh` now always runs the bundle build before installing, so the installed app matches the branch.
- When a scheme has no handler, the error says so instead of quoting an empty string.
- The earlier `ensureDefault` logic stays. It snapshots handlers, reports "already set" or "set now", and trusts the actual handler after each `set` call.
- Agents do not run the real `default set`. The user verifies that step on a real Mac.

## Rejected
- `make clean && make install` as a one-off workaround. It would fix only this run, and the script would stay broken for later installs.

